- C places the onus of giving back any dynamically allocated memory on the programmer.

- Modern languages like Java, Javascript, and Python keep track of when we stop dynamic memory layer that can automatically reclaim the memory.

- The more difficult problem after a series of calls to malloc() and free() the heap space becomes fragmented and the clean up is needed. The Clean up is called "garbage collection".

